    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature end-to-end, following the repository's existing conventions for derived owner fields (like `displayName`, `initials`, etc.).\n\n**What the change does:** `POST /api/owners` now accepts an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR); `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns a derived, read-only `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title was supplied.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 the API contract that DTOs are generated from:\n   - Added `title` (optional enum MR/MRS/MS/DR) to the `OwnerFields` schema (input).\n   - Added `salutation` (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema (output).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persistent `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, so the salutation can be recomposed at read time.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression that derives `salutation` from the owner's title and last name, matching how the other derived fields are declared. (`title` maps automatically by name between DTO and entity.)\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table in all four DB schemas (tests use hsqldb; the app defaults to h2).\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the new `coreComposesSalutation` acceptance test (which asserts `salutation` == `\"DR who\"`) passes, and it's the only test class in the repo.",
